---
description: Graphify codebase navigation
alwaysApply: true
---

This project uses Graphify for codebase navigation. Its local graph is stored in graphify-out/.

Before broad codebase exploration or multi-file changes:
- `graphify query "<specific question>" --budget 500` — understand relevant architecture.
- `graphify explain "<symbol or file>"` — inspect relationships.
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — trace dependencies.
- `graphify affected "<symbol or file>"` — identify potentially impacted code.

Use targeted Read, Grep, Glob, and terminal commands after graph orientation. Always verify actual source files before editing.

After meaningful structural code changes, run `graphify update .`.

Never use paid AI extraction unless explicitly authorized.